<!--
  Intentionally empty, and intentionally not importing the repo-root
  Directory.Build.props.

  better-sqlite3 13 ships prebuilt binaries but keeps a binding.gyp, so npm's
  implicit `node-gyp rebuild` still runs on install. On Windows that generates
  build/binding.sln under node_modules/better-sqlite3 and hands it to MSBuild.
  MSBuild then walks up looking for Directory.Build.props, finds the repo-root
  one, and applies Reactor's whole C# build, which fails with NETSDK1004
  against src/Reactor.Analyzers because nothing has been restored. `npm ci` in
  this folder dies as a result.

  This file stops that walk at the service directory. There is no MSBuild
  project here (the HeadTrax WinUI app lives in ../HeadTrax/ and is
  unaffected), so stopping traversal costs nothing and keeps `npm ci` working
  on Windows. Directory.Build.targets alongside it does the same for the
  targets pass.
-->
<Project>
</Project>
